<title>USA: AMEX to list LEAPS on Cabletron Systems.</title>
<headline>AMEX to list LEAPS on Cabletron Systems.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The American Stock Exchange (AMEX) said on Thursday it would trade long term equity anticipation securities, or LEAPS, on shares of Cabletron Systems from September 23.</p>
<p>One set of LEAPS would expire in January 1998 and another in January 1999. Initial strike prices would be 60, 75 and 95.</p>
<p>Cabletron shares were down 2-3/8 at 70 Thursday afternoon.</p>
<p>The AMEX said Kalb, Voorhis &amp; Co/Cranmer &amp; Cranmer Inc would be the specialist unit for the LEAPS.</p>
<p>--Chicago derivatives desk, (312) 408-8750</p>
<p>E-mail: derivatives@reuters.com</p>
